.TH WHO 1 2026-09-25 "Substrate" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
who \- show who is logged on
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B who
.RB [ \-b ]
.RB [ \-H ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B who
reads the utmp file and prints one line for each
.B USER_PROCESS
record: the login name, the terminal line, and the login time as
.IR YYYY \- MM \- DD " " hh : mm
in local time.
If a remote host is recorded, it is appended in parentheses.
Non-printable characters in these fields are shown as
.BR ? .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-b
Print the time of the last system boot (the
.B BOOT_TIME
record) instead of the logged-in users.
.TP
.B \-H
Print a column heading line first.
.PP
Options must be given as separate arguments.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 2
An unknown argument was given.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /var/run/utmp
Current login records.
.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
$ who \-H
NAME      LINE         TIME              COMMENT
root      tty1         2026\-09\-25 10:02
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR id (1),
.BR uptime (1),
.BR w (1),
.BR whoami (1),
.BR utmp (5)
